# quasar_mode_wind on its own with R4's flags on the real R4 central of bh_cgm_r4_snap32_central
# (Snap_32, Regime 0), with that fixture's accreted mass.
# galaxy 0: R4 reference
# /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R4/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256
# 2b606ee7ac82559e32c7c91161f1edb44f89288ec57016e80da884e118ed0807), Snap_32 row 27 (GalaxyIndex 94,
# Type 0, Regime 0)
# End-of-snapshot output values used as plausible call inputs, not reconstructed call-time state:
# the writer's verbatim floats (ICS the output's IntraClusterStars, DiskScaleRadius its DiskRadius,
# MassLoading the stale value SAGE26 left, which no burst writes), Regime the R4 classifier's.
# Constructed: the stored SnapNum (the output snapshot) and its redshift ZZ[SnapNum] = 1/AA - 1
# (R/src/core_init.c:66), deltaMvir (+2% of Mvir), MergTime, OutflowRate 0, TimeOfLast*Merger -1
# (SAGE26's creation sentinel) and zero histories.
# Reachability: R4-reachable.
# R4's flags (par/R4.par): CGMrecipeOn 1 (:54), FIREmodeOn 1 (:55), SFprescription 1 (:48),
# BulgeSizeOn 3 (:109), SupernovaRecipeOn 1 (:50), DiskInstabilityOn 1 (:52), AGNrecipeOn 2 (:49);
# every other parameter R3's (R4.par differs from R3.par only at :7 and :54).
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine quasar_mode_wind

